[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Zitadel has been installed.

1. PREPARE POSTGRESQL
   Zitadel can initialize its own database. Ensure PostgreSQL is running
   and accessible via the credentials in %%ETCDIR%%/zitadel.yaml.

   Alternatively, create the database manually:
     sudo -u postgres createuser zitadel
     sudo -u postgres createdb -O zitadel zitadel

2. CONFIGURE
   Edit the configuration file:
     edit %%ETCDIR%%/zitadel.yaml

3. SET THE MASTER KEY (required, exactly 32 characters)
     sysrc zitadel_masterkey="$(openssl rand -base64 24)"

4. ENABLE AND START
     sysrc zitadel_enable="YES"
     service zitadel start

5. CONNECT
   Management Console: http://localhost:8080/ui/console
   Health check:       http://localhost:8080/debug/healthz

   For production use, configure TLS or use a reverse proxy.
   Documentation: https://zitadel.com/docs/self-hosting/manage/configure
EOM
}
]
